-      "id": "US-829",
-      "title": "Emit WhatsApp typing indicator during AI processing delay",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "When Rainbow AI receives a WhatsApp message and begins processing, send a typing indicator (chat presence 'composing') to the sender immediately, then clear it when the reply is sent. Without this, users see dead silence for 2-6 seconds between sending and receiving a reply, causing perceived unresponsiveness and drop-offs.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "On every incoming WhatsApp message, `sendWhatsAppTypingIndicator` is called with `composing` state before pipeline processing begins",
-        "Typing indicator is cleared (paused state sent) immediately when the bot reply is dispatched",
-        "If processing takes over 20 seconds the indicator is re-sent to prevent WhatsApp's 25-second auto-dismiss",
-        "Typing indicator is NOT sent if the message is silently dropped (duplicate, system message, or ignored group message)",
-        "Behaviour is configurable per-profile via settings.json `features.typingIndicator: true|false`"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "`sendWhatsAppTypingIndicator` already exists in `src/lib/whatsapp/index.ts` — integrate into `src/assistant/message-router.ts` before pipeline dispatch",
-        "Baileys API: `sock.sendPresenceUpdate('composing', jid)` and `sock.sendPresenceUpdate('paused', jid)`",
-        "Gate behind `delay > 500ms` check to avoid unnecessary presence updates for instant cached replies"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "small",
-      "passes": true
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "US-830",
-      "title": "Baileys circuit breaker: long cooldown after consecutive reconnect failures",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "The current reconnect logic (3 attempts, max 60s delay) is insufficient to prevent WhatsApp account bans caused by rapid connect/disconnect cycling. When the supervisor and Baileys instance both retry simultaneously, hundreds of failed handshakes can trigger abuse detection. A circuit breaker must open after N consecutive failures and enforce a 30-minute cooldown.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "After 5 consecutive connection failures (configurable), the circuit opens and no further reconnection is attempted for 30 minutes",
-        "A WARNING-level log is emitted: `[Baileys:id] Circuit breaker OPEN — 5 consecutive failures. Cooling down for 30 min.`",
-        "An admin WhatsApp notification is sent when the circuit opens",
-        "After the 30-minute cooldown the circuit enters HALF-OPEN, attempts one reconnection, and either closes (success) or reopens with another 30-min cooldown",
-        "Circuit state (open/closed/half-open, last-open timestamp, failure count) is exposed on `GET /api/rainbow/status` per instance"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Implement inside `src/lib/whatsapp/instance.ts` `handleDisconnect()` — replace current 3-attempt counter with a circuit-breaker state machine",
-        "Separate from `baileys-supervisor.ts` which handles supervisor-level crashes — this is instance-level connection cycling",
-        "Use `Date.now()` timestamps rather than a library; no external dependency needed"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": true
-    },
